 "pdf": "ads127l11.pdf",
 "pages": "p.3 (pins), p.5 (ROC), p.10-11 (timing), p.27-28 (data rates), p.44-47 (reset, control modes), p.49-56 (SPI, commands, data), p.60-68 (registers)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog input, buffers, reference, VCM, input range, offset/gain calibration registers (stored only)",
  "16-bit resolution (CONFIG4.DATA = 1), the optional STATUS header byte (CONFIG4.STATUS) and SPI CRC byte: the output frame is always the 24-bit data; register-map CRC check, SPI_ERR / REG_ERR never set",
  "3-wire SPI (CS tied low, CS_MODE) and the 1024-ones SPI reset pattern; daisy-chain pass-through",
  "synchronized control mode (START_MODE = 10b) converts continuously regardless of START: the model only starts on the START pin / START bit; start/stop mode stops immediately rather than after the ongoing conversion",
  "a register write to 04h-0Eh restarting the conversion; conversion-start DELAY and the filter latency of the first conversion (conversion time is the steady 1 / data rate for SPEED_MODE and FILTER at fCLK 25.6 / 3.2 MHz, fMOD = fCLK / 2)",
  "CLK_SEL / CLK_DIV clocking (the CLK pin is not used), standby and power-down (PWDN bit) modes, OUT_DRV",
  "REV_ID reset is xxh (0 here); ALV_FLAG, ADC_ERR, MOD_FLAG never set; CS_MODE reads 0",
  "DRDY high pulse before new data when data are not read; one-shot mode keeps DRDY low during readback (modeled as cleared on read)"
 ],
 "variants": "ADS117L11 is the 16-bit sibling (own datasheet); the ADS127L11 datasheet also shows a RUK WQFN-20 package that has no orderable part in the skeleton",
